GaryOlson <nethack@garyolson.org> wrote:
>
> Patric
> Rather than a single line of characters all crammed together in an
> easy-to-fubar string, could you break each special character in to its
> own definition line?
> boulder = 0
> potion = !
> etc

I am not that intimate with the code that would be affected by such an
option.

But I've looked in the past how bouldersym is implemented and
that's why i'm a bit afraid that there are a lot of edge cases and
that it would be a bitch to get it right (if this is even possible).

> This would allow for a greater use of the ANSI character scheme;
> especially for those non-Western font countries.

Doesn't OPTIONS=dungeon:[...] already support characters > 127 and <
255?

UTF-8 is not even a possible as the way NetHack is structured only
works with fixed 1 char encodings.

You can of course assign an UTF-8 encoded name to your pet and that
will even work. But in the course of the game you will see that this
name will sometimes screw up the screen output a little bit.

